; Lead: BrokkAi/bifrost-packs#167 (CVE-2026-96230, GHSA-qjpx-jqm5-h2c4),
; affected-version part.
; OSV: NuGet Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server introduced 8.0.0
; fixed 8.0.32, introduced 9.0.0 fixed 9.0.21, introduced 10.0.0 fixed 10.0.13,
; introduced 11.0.0-preview.1 fixed 11.0.0-rc.2.
; Product source contract: UseWebAssemblyDebugging(this IApplicationBuilder app)
; maps the /_framework/debug endpoints of the WebAssembly debug proxy. In the
; affected releases those endpoints reflect exception text without encoding.
; The advisory affects every call on an affected release, including a call
; guarded by IsDevelopment(), so this rule does not inspect guards.
;
; Engine contract: declarations from
; semantic-packs/dotnet/bifrost.dotnet.aspnetcore-webassembly-server-csharp.json.
; Its `affected` and `fixed` shards declare the same extension method. Each
; activates only from restored NuGet evidence (obj/project.assets.json and the
; package assembly in an approved package folder) that selects a version in its
; ranges. A call is reported when its exact binding is to the affected record.
; bifrost.dotnet.aspnetcore-hosting-csharp supplies the hosting types.
;
; Incomplete evidence stays incomplete. Without restore output no shard
; activates and the call stays unbound, so the run is not clean. Versions before
; 8.0.0 are outside the advisory record and activate neither shard. A solution
; whose projects restore both an affected and a fixed version activates both
; shards (ambiguous identity). On Bifrost 0.15.2 the extension binds on an
; IApplicationBuilder receiver and in the explicit static form. A WebApplication
; receiver, including minimal-hosting `var app = builder.Build()`, stays
; callee_unresolved and leaves the run inconclusive rather than clean.
; Not covered: an unguarded call on a fixed version (outside the advisory).
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.security.csharp.webassembly-debugging-affected-version"
  :name "WebAssembly debugging middleware on an affected ASP.NET Core release"
  :message "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server before 8.0.32, 9.0.21 or 10.0.13 reflects unencoded exception text from /_framework/debug (CVE-2026-96230); upgrade the package"
  :severity warning
  :description "Reports UseWebAssemblyDebugging calls in a project that restores an affected Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server release (8.0.0 to 8.0.31, 9.0.0 to 9.0.20, 10.0.0 to 10.0.12, or 11.0.0-preview.1 up to 11.0.0-rc.2). In those releases the WebAssembly debug proxy endpoint reflects exception text without encoding (CVE-2026-96230, GHSA-qjpx-jqm5-h2c4). An IsDevelopment() guard does not remove the report: the fix is the package upgrade. Missing NuGet restore evidence leaves the run incomplete rather than clean."
  :help-uri "https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/security/advisories/GHSA-qjpx-jqm5-h2c4"
  :tags ["security" "csharp" "aspnetcore" "blazor" "xss" "cve-2026-96230" "cwe-79"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name debugging
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (resolved-call :resolves-to "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder.WebAssemblyNetDebugProxyAppBuilderExtensions.UseWebAssemblyDebugging" :proof declared
          (call-bindings
            (call-shape
              (language csharp
                (call :callee (name "UseWebAssemblyDebugging"))))))))
    (group :name by-call :by (debugging.site_id)
      (aggregate :name affected :op count
        :where ((debugging.model_record_id in (
          "member.dotnet.aspnetcore-webassembly-server-csharp.affected.usewebassemblydebugging")))))
    (assert :group by-call :value affected :cardinality (exactly 0)))
  :classification (classification
    :fallback (classification-id :taxonomy "CWE" :id "79")))
